Let a frontend list the error console's entries with the item that raised each

The editor's error console is text in pieces with colours (signal_errorConsolePrint). A frontend that shows the
errors as a list, and takes the player to the trigger or script that raised one, needs each entry whole and which
item it was; the text names an item only by its name, which need not be unique.

- Host::signal_errorConsoleEntry carries each entry signal_errorConsolePrint prints, in its parts: a Lua error's
  object, function and message (TLuaInterpreter::logError()), an event handler's event and message
  (logEventError()), a printError()'s function info and message (errorc()), and a debugc()'s text (debug()).
- THeadlessSession::errorConsoleEntry sends each, after its errorConsoleText pieces, as an ErrorConsoleEntry: its
  parts, when, and the item that raised it as scriptItems() names it, where the function is one of the editor's
  items (Trigger12, Alias3, Timer5, Key2, Action4) or the message's chunk ("[string \"Script: name\"]:3:") names
  exactly one item of its kind by its name, with the line of that item's Lua the message names. A temporary item,
  which the editor does not show, is none.
- docs/headless.md describes it.

Tested by Mudlet/android's native/tests/test_mudlet_engine.py (error_console: a trigger's Lua error with the trigger
and its line, an event handler's with its script, Lua run from the frontend and a temporary trigger's with none, a
debugc()). The desktop is unchanged: nothing connects the new signal.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.
Upstream: not opened yet

